# Source of truth for direct dependencies. Resolved versions are pinned in
# requirements.txt, which is what Render installs.
#
# To regenerate:
#   .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.in
#   .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pip freeze > requirements.txt

# Web
fastapi
uvicorn[standard]

# Config
pydantic
pydantic-settings
python-dotenv

# Database
sqlalchemy[asyncio]
asyncpg
alembic

# Auth
authlib
itsdangerous
httpx

# JWT verification for the Better Auth cutover. `pyjwt` and `cryptography`
# were BOTH already resolved transitively, and that is exactly why they are
# listed -- the same argument that promoted python-multipart, langchain-openai
# and pandas/numpy above. `app/auth/jwt.py` imports them BY NAME to verify
# every request's identity, so a future dependency bump that drops either one
# would not fail the build; it would 401 every signed-in user in production,
# nowhere near the change that caused it. The [crypto] extra is not optional:
# Better Auth signs with EdDSA (Ed25519), which pyjwt cannot verify without
# `cryptography` and which it reports as an unsupported ALGORITHM rather than
# as a missing package.
pyjwt[crypto]

# RAG: chains, splitters, and the three provider integrations.
#
# langchain-text-splitters is listed explicitly on purpose. Under langchain 0.x
# it arrived as a transitive dependency of `langchain`; under 1.x it does not,
# and `from langchain.text_splitter import ...` raises ModuleNotFoundError.
langchain
langchain-text-splitters
langchain-google-genai
langchain-pinecone
langchain-cohere

# The OpenRouter client. `ChatOpenAI` and `OpenAIEmbeddings` pointed at
# openrouter.ai are OpenAI-PROTOCOL clients, not calls to OpenAI -- no
# OPENAI_API_KEY is needed and nothing here talks to OpenAI. It was already
# installed as a langchain-pinecone transitive, which is exactly why it is listed
# now: app/rag/llm.py and app/rag/retriever.py both import it directly, so a
# future change to langchain-pinecone's dependencies would otherwise break every
# chat model AND every embedding call in the project with an ImportError nowhere
# near the cause.
#
# As of 2026-08-16 it carries BOTH halves of the model layer. `langchain-google-genai`
# above no longer stays for embeddings -- those moved to OpenRouter, same model
# and same 768d space, no re-ingest. It stays solely as the ROLLBACK route
# selected by `settings.embedding_route = "google"`, which is why removing it is
# a decision about rollback rather than a cleanup.
langchain-openai

# ContextualCompressionRetriever -- the class PRD section 3.5 names as the Stage 1
# -> Stage 2 wrapper -- moved out of `langchain` in the 1.x split and now lives
# here. Keeping the canonical class is worth one extra package: the workshop
# teaches this exact wrapping, and hand-rolling the equivalent would make the
# stage change look like bespoke code rather than the one-liner it is.
langchain-classic

# Document loading. Only pypdf is needed on top of the stdlib: markdown and
# text are read directly. Originals ARE now kept, in object storage rather than
# on disk -- but they are kept as bytes and never re-parsed from a path, so this
# stays the whole document-loading surface.
pypdf

# MCP tools as LangChain tools. Nothing imports this yet -- it is here so the
# Stage 2 agent can be given real tools without a dependency change mid-build.
langchain-mcp-adapters

# Multipart form parsing, required by FastAPI's UploadFile. It was already
# present in the venv, but only transitively via mcp <- langchain-mcp-adapters --
# a package the comment above admits nothing imports yet. Removing that package
# would have killed every upload route at import time with a RuntimeError about
# a missing dependency, nowhere near the change that caused it. Direct now.
python-multipart

# Stage 3 measurement. Ragas scores faithfulness, answer relevance, context
# precision and context recall against the golden set.
ragas

# The `run_python` sandbox's toolkit -- the four libraries the generated code is
# allowed to import, and therefore the four the sandbox subprocess must be able
# to resolve. They are listed here rather than left to chance because the model
# is told in its tool description that it may import them: an absent one is not
# an ImportError the developer sees, it is a tool call that fails at runtime
# inside a subprocess, surfacing as a handout stuck at "failed" with a traceback
# nobody reads.
#
# matplotlib and python-pptx are genuinely new (~55 MB on the Render build).
# matplotlib runs on the `Agg` backend -- no GUI toolkit, no display -- which is
# what keeps that number to 55 MB rather than to a desktop stack.
matplotlib
python-pptx

# pandas and numpy are ALREADY INSTALLED, as transitive dependencies of ragas.
# They are promoted to DIRECT dependencies here anyway, and that is the whole
# point of the two lines: the sandbox imports them BY NAME, so a future change to
# ragas' dependency tree -- a version that drops pandas, or swaps it for polars --
# would silently remove them from this project. Nothing at build time would
# complain, because nothing this repo wrote imports them at module scope; the
# failure would appear later, as generated code raising ModuleNotFoundError
# inside a subprocess, nowhere near the ragas bump that caused it. Exactly the
# argument that promoted `python-multipart` and `langchain-openai` above.
pandas
numpy

# NOT optional, and NOT a stale pin to bump. `ragas/llms/base.py` imports
# `langchain_community.chat_models.vertexai` at module scope, and
# langchain-community 0.4.x DELETED that module -- so the newest ragas and the
# newest langchain-community cannot be installed together, and `import ragas`
# fails with a ModuleNotFoundError naming a package this project never imports.
# Every ragas release from 0.2.15 to 0.4.3 carries that import, so downgrading
# ragas does not help; the pin has to go here. 0.3.x does not drag langchain-core
# back below 1.x, so the rest of the stack is unaffected.
langchain-community<0.4

# Object storage. **An S3-PROTOCOL client pointed at Cloudflare R2 -- nothing
# here calls AWS**, there is no AWS account, and no AWS_* environment variable is
# read: `app/storage.py` passes the R2_* credentials explicitly, and they are
# named that way precisely so botocore's ambient credential chain cannot pick up
# something else from `~/.aws/config` by accident.
#
# Exactly the relationship `langchain-openai` above has with OpenRouter, where
# the same note has now survived two model migrations. R2 serves no API of its
# own for objects -- the S3 protocol IS Cloudflare's interface -- so this is the
# client, not a choice of vendor.
boto3

# The Google ADK agent runtime (change set 18), selected by AGENT_RUNTIME.
#
# **`litellm` is deliberately NOT here, and that is the whole design.** ADK's
# documented road to a non-Gemini provider is `google.adk.models.lite_llm.LiteLlm`,
# and this project does not take it: `app/adk/model.py` is a ~30-line `BaseLlm`
# that delegates to `app/rag/llm.build_chat_model`, so every measured OpenRouter
# workaround AND the metering attachment are inherited rather than re-derived.
# Taking the litellm road would have re-introduced `max_completion_tokens` (a
# guaranteed 404 here), an unremovable deprecated `stream_options`, and an
# unmetered call site that `metering_check` case 12 would have printed green over.
#
# Measured cost of this line: 8 new distributions and ONE version bump
# (google-genai 2.18.1 -> 2.20.0). It does not disturb langchain 1.x, the
# `langchain-community<0.4` pin ragas needs, or pinecone.
google-adk
